			factPattern: "<span class='bar-tag'>2026 BAR EXAM — Q.1</span> A group called the Sha Group gathers signatures for a people's initiative petition to change the 1987 Constitution. The petition seeks to amend Sections 1 to 7 of Article VI (Legislative Department) and Sections 1 to 4 of Article VII (Executive Department), changing the government from a Bicameral-Presidential system to a Unicameral-Parliamentary system. Sha Group claims more than 6.3 million signatures, equal to at least 12% of all registered voters, with at least 3% coming from every legislative district. Sha Group files a petition with the COMELEC asking for a plebiscite to ratify these proposed changes.",
