			factPattern: "<span class='bar-tag'>2026 BAR EXAM — Q.2</span> PAGCOR, using its power under its own charter (P.D. 1869), decides to expand its casino operations by leasing and renovating part of a hotel in San Fernando City. Conservative groups in the city oppose this. The Sangguniang Panlungsod then passes two ordinances: (1) one refusing to issue business permits to any establishment used even partly for casino operations, and (2) another completely banning casino operations within the city, with fines, closure, and imprisonment for violators. PAGCOR and the hotel owner ask the court to strike down both ordinances as ultra vires and as violating local autonomy.",
