			factPattern: "<span class='bar-tag'>2026 BAR EXAM — Q.3</span> Congress passes an appropriation law. Following requests from DPWH officials, this law lets individual legislators decide, after the law is already enacted, exactly how much money goes to specific flood control projects, and who the beneficiaries or contractors will be. The DBM later releases funds based on these individual legislators' instructions. A Senate investigation reveals that many flood control contracts went to companies owned by the legislators' relatives or endorsed by them, that large kickbacks were paid to legislators who 'inserted' these projects, and that many of the projects turned out to be ghost, unfinished, abandoned, or substandard.",
