			factPattern: "<span class='bar-tag'>2026 BAR EXAM — Q.4</span> To address concerns about executive privilege in Senate investigations of corruption, the President issues Executive Order No. 111 (E.O. 111). E.O. 111 sets rules for question hour and legislative inquiries, defines the scope of executive privilege, and lists specific executive officials covered. It also provides that none of the named officials may appear before any congressional investigation without the President's prior approval. The Senate, through the Senate President, asks the Supreme Court to declare E.O. 111 unconstitutional.",
